WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.591
RUFUS: The open question — and it stays
open because the sources don't

00:00:03.591 --> 00:00:07.181
RUFUS: resolve it — is whether any
public body is positioned to audit

00:00:07.181 --> 00:00:10.771
RUFUS: what Daybreak actually delivers
at the end of those six months. Or

00:00:10.771 --> 00:00:14.362
RUFUS: whether the receipt simply never
arrives.

00:00:14.482 --> 00:00:18.506
ALEX: And if no one's required to check,
no one will know what

00:00:18.506 --> 00:00:22.531
ALEX: was actually purchased with that
billion dollars. Or who's holding the
keys.

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:27.085
ALEX: Here's the question I haven't
asked yet. Nvidia just paid $13 billion

00:00:27.085 --> 00:00:31.518
ALEX: for a platform with documented
security incidents. Does that change
what "subsidized

00:00:31.518 --> 00:00:35.952
ALEX: access" actually means for a
defender who's now downstream of that?
